<Answer>
40 investors — predominantly male (25/40) — show clear preference hierarchy: **PPF (2.03) > Mutual Funds (2.55) > Equity (3.47) > Fixed Deposits (3.57)** when ranking 1=best. Gold and Debentures rank lowest (>5.7).

**Drivers:** Returns dominates (25/40), followed by Risk (14). 30/40 cite Capital Appreciation for Equity. Objectives are Capital Appreciation (26) and Growth (11).

**Demographic splits:** Gender barely differentiates objectives (66% of females vs 64% of males seek Cap Appreciation) but males rank PPF even higher (1.84 vs 2.33) and Fixed Deposits higher (3.2 vs 4.2). Correlation between Mutual_Funds and PPF (0.18) suggests conservative investors like both.

Artifacts generated — correlation heatmap, demographics breakdown, investment drivers and ranking charts — plus a full HTML report. Dataset is clean (0 missing) and ready for deeper modeling (e.g., predict Objective from rankings + demographics).
</Answer>
